{c: Verse 1}
[B]Wholl walk me [A]down to church
[G]when Im sixty [F#]years of age
[Em]When the ragged dog they gave me
[F#]has been ten years in the grave
[B]And senorita [A]play guitar,
[G]play it [F#]just for you
[Em]My rosary has broken and
[F#]my beads have [B]all slipped through
[B]Youve hung up [A]your great coat
[G]and youve laid [F#]down your gun
[Em]You know the war you fought
[F#]in wasnt too much fun
[B]And the future [A]youre giving me
[G]holds nothing [F#]for a gun
[Em]Ive no wish to [F#]be living sixty years on
